      },
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "curator_note": "Table 8.2 (p.167, Two bonds cleaved, EE+ i-i with H rearrangement) = the onium reaction. H transfers from the carbon beta to O+ onto the oxygen, the O-C(alpha) bond cleaves, and the C(alpha)=C(beta) alkene is eliminated to give the protonated carbonyl. Book draws 0 curved arrows for this entry (net reactant->product only); both encoded 2-electron moves are implied by the transformation. The book draws the transferring H on the carbon adjacent to the O-CH2 (a 4-membered beta-H transfer, matching the drawn C(alpha)=C(beta) product); longer CnH2n chains would give the usual 6-membered gamma-H onium transfer. Migrating H carried as isotope [1H:10]. Instantiation = ethyl methyleneoxocarbenium (R=H); no m/z / intensity printed -- m/z curator-computed."
    },
