      "curator_note": "No MØD rule encodes the oxygen (oxocarbenium) onium reaction, but IMS_4_43_rH is the exact nitrogen analog: [C]([H])([H])[C]([H])([H])[N+]([H]){=}[C]([H])([H])>>[C]{=}[C].[N+]([H])([H]){=}[C] -- a beta-H transfer to an iminium N+ eliminating an alkene, the same EE+ H-rearrangement/alkene-loss pattern with N in place of O. Chemistry-verified (same bond changes); not RDKit substructure-tested."
